From 235a7074ae134a6c17861dd0e8a84d28dadbba5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Pfeiffer <cpfeiffer@rev-crew.info>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 07:42:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] linux-swap: Require a crypt layer on every branch below
 btrfs devices

A device-mapper or md device can join an encrypted and a plain device,
e.g. a logical volume on a volume group of a LUKS and a plain physical
volume, and swap can land on either. The walker of the other routes
counts such a device as encrypted once it finds one crypt layer below
it, so the btrfs route now walks the devices with its own walker, which
requires a crypt layer on every branch.

The dm/uuid check moves to a helper both walkers use; the walker of the
other routes is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
